# Equality of callable values is reusable without equality of their inputs.
# Run: cargo run --release -- -strict -lang en -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_builtin_strategy/function_value_congruence.lit
# The original cardinality proof had to publish both cartesian memberships,
# release fn_set_member twice and instantiate equal_functions_apply for each
# coordinate (std/cardinality/main.lit, split injectivity proof).
# Boundary: both applications must be well-defined and use equal arguments.
forall Domain,X,Y set,F fn(t Domain) cart(X,Y),a,b Domain:
    F(a)=F(b)
    =>:
        F(a)(1)=F(b)(1)
        F(a)(2)=F(b)(2)
